{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/twfux0ne","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":722.11,"top":567.23,"width":472.53,"height":51.1},"name":"Text 16","text":"Eliminates exit PHI nodes and complex SSA repair by feeding remaining iterations directly to scalar entry.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":18,"typeface":"Exo","color":"#D5D5D5","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/svmt4v6t","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":1240.91,"top":678.06,"width":39.06,"height":19.87},"name":"Text 17","text":"06","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":14,"typeface":"Fira Mono","color":"#9D9D9D","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/x8f69ofe","slideIndex":5,"text":"Our code generation uses a simple, robust pattern: compute the vector iterations via bitmask n & -VF, execute packed instructions in the vector body, and chain the remaining iterations directly into the scalar epilogue without SSA live-out reconstruction."}
